## Homogeneous Trace
Selected endpoint address a_m=ceil(48m/7) has:
  rank_C1(a_m)=1 exactly when 7 divides m
  rank_C1(a_m)=2 otherwise
Thus the HYP-3433 endpoint witness is always in the first two colored
left-corridor high gaps.  The mod-35 color word counts all escapes; the
mod-7 subcolor locates the canonical homogeneous trace inside that set.

## Paris-Harrington / Outer-Extension Reading
bad_phase_counts={'q0_mixed_residues': 4, 'q1_mixed_residues': 0}
The mixed endpoint color is a finite bad branch: it appears only at m=1..4
and is gone after the period extension m -> m+35.  The pure tail is not
fast-growing PH behavior; it is a 35-state automaton with retained colors
(phase, boundary d_r, endpoint rank).  This is the tame AP84 version of the
HYP-2247 rule: do not count colorings without their extension-rank sidecar.

