hamiltonian_path=crt_35_coloring_state -> endpoint_rank_mod7_subcolor -> ph_bad_phase_derivative -> outer_extension_period_shift -> mod35_boundary_color_word -> transition_increment_word -> raw_escape_count -> raw_color_analogy

## Assumption Challenge
Considered vertices: runners, residues mod 35, residues mod 7, high gaps,
color classes, bad-coloring nodes, endpoint addresses, fixed corridors,
and proof obligations.  The chosen quotient preserves AP-tail escape count,
endpoint-witness location, mixed/pure phase, and outer-extension shift.
It destroys arbitrary non-AP wall geometry, so it is a coloring-recursion
sidecar for the AP-tail bridge rather than a global LRC14 proof.
